02_FBM_Clustering/outputs/250_recon/EL*/

# === Last-line catch-all: Thumbs.db anywhere, even inside allowlisted trees ===
# (the ERSP_clean re-include otherwise un-ignores Windows shell preview turds)
**/Thumbs.db

# === Jupyter scratch — never track, even inside the allowlisted outputs trees ===
# (the !.../outputs/**/** allows would otherwise force-include these)
**/.ipynb_checkpoints/
**/.ipynb_checkpoints/**

# No HTML in the analysis repo — web pages live in the lorafanda.github.io repo.
# The pipeline only EXPORTS data (pool_web/*.csv,*.json) that those pages fetch.
*.html
# ...except the committed viewer pages that live here (opened locally / mirrored to Pages).
!poolv2.html
!pool.html
!analysis_status.html

# Pooling viz PNGs are regenerable + heavy; pool.html renders from contacts_pool.csv, not PNGs.
04_FBM_Pooling/outputs/pooling/**/*.png
# ...except the per-role / per-neurosynth-region info-card images, fetched by the web info panel.
!04_FBM_Pooling/outputs/pooling/**/role_cards/*.png
!04_FBM_Pooling/outputs/pooling/**/region_cards/*.png
# ...and the summary figures the whole-pipeline status page (analysis_status.html) embeds.
!04_FBM_Pooling/outputs/pooling/pool_web/hga_timeseries.png
!04_FBM_Pooling/outputs/pooling/pool_web/role_corr.png
!04_FBM_Pooling/outputs/pooling/pool_web/role_onset_ordering.png
!04_FBM_Pooling/outputs/pooling/neurosynth/hga_timeseries.png
!04_FBM_Pooling/outputs/pooling/neurosynth/region_corr.png
!04_FBM_Pooling/outputs/pooling/neurosynth/region_onset_ordering.png
# multi-label attribution matrices ("attribute an electrode to ONE network?") + the
# ERSP x atlas-probability correlation maps (lab-notes Figs 4 and 7-9).
!04_FBM_Pooling/outputs/pooling/neurosynth/attribution_matrix.png
!04_FBM_Pooling/outputs/pooling/pool_web/attribution_matrix.png
!04_FBM_Pooling/outputs/pooling/atlas_corr/*.png
!04_FBM_Pooling/outputs/pooling/atlas_corr/fedorenko/*.png
# hand-drawn figures from the lab meetings, shown in the status page's Meetings tab.
!04_FBM_Pooling/outputs/pooling/meeting_notes/*.png

# Neurosynth input maps (downloaded .nii.gz from neurosynth.org) — heavy, regenerable, never push.
# (The DERIVED region labels/cards under outputs/pooling/neurosynth/ stay tracked.)
04_FBM_Pooling/neurosynth/

# Consensus co-clustering matrices: (n_samples x n_samples) float — ~17 MB EACH and one
# per run. Regenerable by 211_validation, and nothing reads them: MOBA and the status
# site use consensus_heatmap.png + per_cluster_stability.csv, which stay tracked.
**/consensus_matrix.npy

# 390_results: heavy embedded outputs (8.6 MB+) — don't track. Strip outputs to version the code.
03_FBM_Classifying/390_results.ipynb
# Windows thumbnail cache junk
Thumbs.db

# Timestamped backups written by fix_recon_l_vs_I.py --apply (git history is the real record)
*.bak_[0-9]*
# ...and the index.json backup cleanup_stale.py writes before pruning.
*.json.bak

# Spike-sorting outputs: raw acquisition binaries (FBMdata_*.bin is 0.7-1.7 GB EACH,
# far over GitHub's 100 MB hard limit) plus their derived artifacts. Machine-local and
# regenerable from DATARAW by notebook 13 — the NOTEBOOKS stay tracked, the data does not.
01_FBM_Analysis/outputs/13_microSpikeSorting/
01_FBM_Analysis/outputs/13b_microSpikeSorting_notrials/
**/FBMdata_*.bin

# Fedorenko / LanA atlas: downloaded inputs from the Fedorenko lab release, not our
# output. Same treatment as the neurosynth maps above — heavy, re-downloadable, and the
# DERIVED results (atlas_corr figures, the lana_inout run) stay tracked.
04_FBM_Pooling/federenko_atlas/
04_FBM_Pooling/federenko-atlases-archive.zip
